WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.136 --> 00:00:03.139
&gt;&gt;&gt; Out front now, a Russian

00:00:03.139 --> 00:00:05.760
activist and member of pussy

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:08.041
riot jailed for 20 months in

00:00:08.041 --> 00:00:10.176
Russia.
Russia recently opened another

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:11.355
criminal trial against her in

00:00:11.355 --> 00:00:13.257
response to an art show that

00:00:13.257 --> 00:00:15.425
included burning a portrait of

00:00:15.425 --> 00:00:18.695
Putin.
I really appreciate your time.

00:00:18.695 --> 00:00:19.796
You hear some of these Russian

00:00:19.796 --> 00:00:21.898
women saying, one says, I

00:00:21.898 --> 00:00:22.832
support Putin.

00:00:22.832 --> 00:00:24.501
He does everything right, good

00:00:24.501 --> 00:00:25.769
man, we love him.

00:00:25.769 --> 00:00:28.438
Is this the view of most

00:00:28.438 --> 00:00:30.107
Russians even now?

00:00:31.372 --> 00:00:35.143
&gt;&gt; I highly doubt it.

00:00:35.143 --> 00:00:39.247
It's really difficult to measure

00:00:39.247 --> 00:00:40.915
what the public actually thinks

00:00:53.304 --> 00:00:54.873
about Putin because it's

00:00:55.006 --> 00:00:59.077
incredibly costly to criticize

00:00:59.210 --> 00:01:02.213
him.
I've seen a lot of political

00:01:02.347 --> 00:01:03.715
prisoners in Russia appearing

00:01:03.848 --> 00:01:04.783
every day.

00:01:04.783 --> 00:01:06.785
People are getting eight years

00:01:06.785 --> 00:01:09.020
for pushing like button on

00:01:09.154 --> 00:01:09.521
Instagram.

00:01:09.521 --> 00:01:12.056
And it makes it incredibly

00:01:12.190 --> 00:01:13.925
dangerous for people to say

00:01:14.058 --> 00:01:15.393
something against Putin.

00:01:15.527 --> 00:01:20.198
There was a case recently where

00:01:20.331 --> 00:01:21.266
an 11-year-old girl made a

00:01:21.399 --> 00:01:24.803
drawing with a Ukrainian flag,

00:01:24.803 --> 00:01:26.271
and she was -- she's currently

00:01:26.404 --> 00:01:28.807
in foster care, and her dad is

00:01:28.873 --> 00:01:29.374
under arrest.

00:01:29.507 --> 00:01:34.446
&gt;&gt; Foster care and her father

00:01:34.813 --> 00:01:35.447
under arrest?
11 years old.

00:01:35.447 --> 00:01:36.314
It's terrifying.

00:01:36.448 --> 00:01:37.115
That brings it home.

00:01:37.248 --> 00:01:39.184
You know, you know because you

00:01:39.317 --> 00:01:40.819
spent almost two years in a

00:01:40.952 --> 00:01:42.821
Russian prison.

00:01:42.887 --> 00:01:44.456
What happens when you cross

00:01:44.823 --> 00:01:47.225
Putin in any way.

00:01:47.358 --> 00:01:48.827
What risks are people taking now

00:01:48.827 --> 00:01:51.162
to speak out?

00:01:51.296 --> 00:01:53.898
&gt;&gt; They can be arrested.

00:01:54.032 --> 00:01:54.833
Their family members can be

00:01:54.833 --> 00:01:59.270
arrested.

00:01:59.404 --> 00:02:03.942
They can be murdered themselves

00:02:04.075 --> 00:02:06.444
or to other friends of mine who

00:02:06.845 --> 00:02:07.846
died because of criticizing

00:02:07.979 --> 00:02:11.216
Putin and his regime.

00:02:11.349 --> 00:02:13.117
It's -- it's not something that

00:02:13.251 --> 00:02:17.889
I would advise people do, to go

00:02:18.022 --> 00:02:20.391
openly against the war or

00:02:20.525 --> 00:02:22.494
president Putin or at least if

00:02:22.861 --> 00:02:23.995
they are in Russia currently.

00:02:24.128 --> 00:02:25.997
They can make this choice for

00:02:26.130 --> 00:02:28.867
themselves, but I wouldn't

00:02:28.867 --> 00:02:30.869
advise it because it's worse to

00:02:30.935 --> 00:02:32.871
risk your life and the life of

00:02:32.937 --> 00:02:35.173
your relatives.

00:02:35.306 --> 00:02:37.208
That's why whenever Russians are

00:02:37.342 --> 00:02:41.279
being criticized for not doing

00:02:41.412 --> 00:02:42.947
enough, I feel for them because

00:02:43.081 --> 00:02:44.883
a lot of people I know, they

00:02:44.883 --> 00:02:46.885
have to stay in Russia.

00:02:46.885 --> 00:02:49.354
They don't have voice.

00:02:49.487 --> 00:02:52.891
They simply cannot speak out

00:02:52.891 --> 00:02:54.893
against the regime because it

00:02:54.893 --> 00:02:56.394
can be just incredibly

00:02:56.528 --> 00:02:57.662
dangerous, and they also cannot

00:02:57.795 --> 00:03:00.899
leave the country because not

00:03:01.032 --> 00:03:02.967
everyone is privileged enough to

00:03:03.101 --> 00:03:05.403
be able to leave the country and

00:03:05.537 --> 00:03:06.905
start a life somewhere else.

00:03:06.971 --> 00:03:09.207
&gt;&gt; How bad is it being prisoned

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:10.909
in Russia?

00:03:11.009 --> 00:03:13.478
You said you spent the 0 months

00:03:13.611 --> 00:03:14.546
away from a child that you had,

00:03:14.913 --> 00:03:17.782
and you had to serve that time.

00:03:17.916 --> 00:03:20.919
&gt;&gt; It's -- it's really a hell on

00:03:20.919 --> 00:03:22.520
Earth, especially when you're

00:03:22.921 --> 00:03:25.790
being moved to the penal colony

00:03:25.924 --> 00:03:27.625
where you have to work.

00:03:27.759 --> 00:03:29.494
By law, you have to work, and

00:03:29.627 --> 00:03:32.931
it's practically a slave labor.

00:03:33.064 --> 00:03:36.034
Luckily, I was able to fight

00:03:36.167 --> 00:03:37.702
against the system, and years

00:03:37.835 --> 00:03:41.773
later after I got out of jail,

00:03:41.906 --> 00:03:46.311
my prison boss -- ex-prison

00:03:46.444 --> 00:03:50.281
boss -- was sentenced for slave

00:03:50.415 --> 00:03:51.516
labor in the penal colony where

00:03:51.749 --> 00:03:54.953
I served my time, I was forced

00:03:55.053 --> 00:03:56.955
to sew police uniforms.

00:03:56.955 --> 00:03:58.957
These days, people who oppose

00:03:59.090 --> 00:04:00.391
Putin and who say something

00:04:00.525 --> 00:04:01.826
against the war, they are being

00:04:01.960 --> 00:04:03.294
sent to colonies to produce

00:04:03.428 --> 00:04:06.397
military uniforms.

00:04:06.531 --> 00:04:08.499
&gt;&gt; That's incredible irony,

00:04:08.633 --> 00:04:09.500
horrible irony.

00:04:09.767 --> 00:04:12.337
I know you just hosted a benefit

00:04:12.470 --> 00:04:15.607
auction called my body, my

00:04:15.740 --> 00:04:16.975
business.

00:04:16.975 --> 00:04:17.342
It's performance.

00:04:17.342 --> 00:04:19.043
It's punk but also art.

00:04:19.177 --> 00:04:20.244
And this has been crucial to

00:04:20.378 --> 00:04:22.981
you.
The auction is in honor of

00:04:22.981 --> 00:04:24.983
international women's day,

00:04:25.116 --> 00:04:26.985
benefitting reproductive

00:04:26.985 --> 00:04:28.353
organizations worldwide.

00:04:28.486 --> 00:04:30.154
Putin today actually came out

00:04:30.288 --> 00:04:31.823
and spoke about national women's

00:04:31.956 --> 00:04:34.092
day, and I want to play for you

00:04:34.225 --> 00:04:35.927
part of what he said the holiday

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:37.161
means to Russia.

00:04:37.295 --> 00:04:39.297
&gt;&gt; Translator: It is always

00:04:39.430 --> 00:04:41.766
filled with special warmth and

00:04:41.899 --> 00:04:43.468
meaning, kind, joyful, and

00:04:43.601 --> 00:04:47.005
sincere feelings because this

00:04:47.005 --> 00:04:48.640
reverence and respect towards

00:04:49.007 --> 00:04:51.142
women and motherhood is an

00:04:51.275 --> 00:04:52.410
unconventional value for us,

00:04:52.543 --> 00:04:53.678
something we have been passing

00:04:53.811 --> 00:04:55.480
on from generation to

00:04:55.613 --> 00:04:56.314
generation.

00:04:56.447 --> 00:04:57.482
&gt;&gt; That was today.

00:04:57.615 --> 00:05:00.218
&gt;&gt; Such a clown.

00:05:00.351 --> 00:05:01.919
&gt;&gt; That's really all there is to

00:05:02.053 --> 00:05:05.023
say.
&gt;&gt; Pretty much.

00:05:05.023 --> 00:05:07.025
&gt;&gt; Well, I appreciate your

00:05:07.125 --> 00:05:09.027
taking the time and talking to

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:09.761
me.
&gt;&gt; Thank you.

00:05:09.761 --> 00:05:11.262
&gt;&gt; You say what you have to say.

